// sharkninja-mkt-data.js
// SharkNinja (NYSE: SN) · Deep Dive ▸ Marketing Strategy — the frozen data behind the tab.
//
// What it is: how SharkNinja's marketing model evolved from the Jul 2023 spin-off to today
// (Goldman Sachs Global Consumer & Retail conference, Sep 15 2026): the spend series from the
// filings against every spend figure said on stage, five eras of the model, the social /
// social-commerce record, the launch and country-entry playbooks, and a curated statement log.
//
// FROZEN. Retrieved once through Quartr (13 earnings calls Q2 2023–Q2 2026, 13 investor
// conferences Sep 2023–Sep 2026, 14 investor decks Jul 2023–Aug 2026) and SEC filings (F-1 Jun
// 2023, 20-F FY2023 and FY2024, 10-K FY2025), on Sep 15 2026. No runtime calls. Quotes are
// verbatim from the transcripts/decks at the Quartr url on each item (deck text normalized only
// for extractor spacing). Net sales FY2022–FY2025 come from js/results-data/sn.js; FY2020–FY2021
// net sales were not in the captures and are left null.
//
// Caveats worth keeping:
// · Spoken spend is not the filings' line. "Advertising costs" (notes to the accounts) were
//   $409.2M / $585.3M / $632.9M in FY2023–25. On stage: "nearly 8.5%" (Jan 2024), "about 9.5%"
//   (Jun 2024), "about 11%" (Sep/Dec 2024), "$600 million +" for FY2024 (reported $585.3M),
//   "$700 million a year … over 11%" (Sep 2025; FY2025 reported 9.9%), "over $800 million a year
//   on marketing and advertising" (Sep 2026, a wider label). The % figures here that are marked
//   "computed" are advertising ÷ net sales; the filings never state that ratio.
// · Advertising growth slowed hard: +$145.3M (FY2023), +$176.1M (FY2024), +$47.6M (FY2025).
// · TikTok Shop start is told three ways: first sale Aug 2025 (CEO, Sep 2026); social commerce
//   "starting from zero 15 months ago" (CEO, Jun 2026 → ~Mar 2025); "zero in the year ago period"
//   for 2Q25 (Q2 2026 call), while the CFO said in May 2026 SN was "starting to annualize" it.
// · No share of sales has ever been given for TikTok Shop, social commerce or D2C (refused until
//   a full year of selling, Sep 2026).
// · Ninja Swirl pre-launch impressions: 60M (prepared) vs 70M (Q&A, same call) vs 75M (BofA).
//   SLUSHi DTC waitlist peak: >200,000 (Q3 2024 call) vs >175,000 (deck, same day).
// · Media leverage: CFO "a massive area of leverage" (Feb 2026) vs CEO "I don't think … we're
//   gonna get media leverage … on a long-term basis" (May 2026).
// · Seeding: ~100 influencers (Feb 2025) vs "about 15, 20" CREAMi influencers for Swirl (May 2025).
// · Category label drift: management says "categories" and "subcategories" interchangeably.
//   Speaker names are normalized (Patraic Reagan appears as "Patrick Regan" in one transcript);
//   the Q4 2025 call's first Q&A answer is garbled, so its TikTok Shop item carries no quote.
// · The log is curated (~175 of ~470 captured statements): near-duplicates merged, keeping the
//   first telling, the latest, or the one with the number.

