    read: 'On stage the intensity ran ahead of the accounts from mid-2024: "about 11%" in Sep and Dec 2024 against 10.6% reported for FY2024, "$600 million +" against $585.3M, and "$700 million … over 11%" in Sep 2025 against <b>$632.9M and 9.9%</b> for FY2025. The dollars still rise, but the increment collapsed: advertising-related expense grew <b>+$145.3M</b> in FY2023, <b>+$176.1M</b> in FY2024 and only <b>+$47.6M</b> in FY2025, when delivery/distribution (+$66.1M) and personnel (+$64.5M) grew faster. S&M as a whole kept climbing to 22.8% of sales, so the growth in "marketing" is now more people, in-house creators and D2C fulfilment than bought media. The Sep 2026 "over $800 million" is "marketing and advertising", a wider label than the filings\' advertising costs, so it is not a like-for-like jump.'
